  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening The Accounting Profession in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development Objective:  The grant aims to strengthen Indonesian accounting profession through supporting Indonesian Institute of Accountants (IAI) to meet the international standards for professional accountants by developing Professional examination program and Continuing Professional Education (CPE) for accountants. The grant will further strengthen the accounting environment in the country by review and improving the implementation of accounting standards for non-public interest entities. Task Description: The project can be divided into 3 main components: A.   Component 1: Development of pathway of professional accountant examination. 1.   Standard operating procedures for the exam will be developed. Syllabus, test bank, and self-study modules for professional accountant examination will also be developed. 2.   Socialization of professional accountant examination through IAI. B.   Component 2: Development of Continuing Professional Education (CPE) for professional accountant through e-learning system Design and develop CPE consists of e-learning system and provide on-line materials. The e-learning system will be developed with linkage to membership administration system to monitor the fulfillment of minimum required CPE hours. C.   Component 3: Review of implementation of the accounting standard for non-public interest entities (SAK-ETAP) issued in 2009. The objective of this component is to review the existing standard to assess the compliance by small and medium enterprises and study their obstacles to comply. Based on recommendations provided from the assessment, further support will be provided to adjust the standards, conduct public hearing and disseminate the standards. The proposed grant will be implemented in 2 years.</narrative>
  </description>
